## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical backpressure control, multi-region rollout, observability, and safe rollback with concrete metrics.

## Key Concepts

- Backpressure and queueing signals
- Auto-tuning concurrency via closed-loop control
- Circuit breakers and safe rollouts
- Cross-region canaries and feature flags
- Observability: p95 latency, backlog, error rate

## Code Example

```javascript
// Adaptive limiter sketch
class AdaptiveLimiter {
  constructor(targetP95 = 300, maxConns = 200) {
    this.targetP95 = targetP95;
    this.maxConns = maxConns;
    this.currConns = Math.floor(maxConns * 0.6);
  }
  onMetrics(p95, backlog) {
    // simple proportional rule; can be replaced by PID
    if (p95 < this.targetP95 && backlog < 0.8 * 5000) {
      this.currConns = Math.min(this.currConns + 5, this.maxConns);
    } else {
      this.currConns = Math.max(this.currConns - 5, 1);
    }
  }
}
``` 

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate the controller with synthetic load and canaries?
- How do you account for clock skew and regional differences in latency metrics?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to design isolation, backpressure controls, and controlled degradation under burst traffic, with clear rollback criteria and observability.

## Key Concepts

- Tenant isolation via edge throttling and per-tenant queues
- Backpressure mechanisms and circuit breakers
- Safe degradation strategies and cache fallbacks
- Telemetry: p95/p99 latency, error rate, queue depth, saturation
- Clear rollback criteria and automation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Simple token bucket limiter
class TokenBucket {
  constructor(rate, capacity) {
    this.rate = rate;
    this.capacity = capacity;
    this.tokens = capacity;
    this.last = Date.now();
  }
  allow() {
    const now = Date.now();
    const elapsed = (now - this.last) / 1000;
    this.tokens = Math.min(this.capacity, this.tokens + elapsed * this.rate);
    this.last = now;
    if (this.tokens >= 1) {
      this.tokens -= 1;
      return true;
    }
    return false;
  }
}
```

